{"name":"Spanish Sky Blue","hex":"#00fffe","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"spanish","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To subject to spanishing, a printing process in which an ink is deposited on the bottoms and sides of depressions formed in a plastic material"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spanish"},{"term":"sky","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Sikaiana."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The atmosphere above a given point, especially as visible from the surface of the Earth as the place where the sun, moon, stars, and clouds are seen.","With a descriptive word: the part of the sky which can be seen from a specific place or at a specific time; its climate, condition, etc."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sky"},{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sky blue","blocks":[{"text":"Sky blue refers to a collection of shades comparable to that of a clear daytime sky. Typically it is a shade of cyan or light teal, though some iterations are closer to light azure or light blue. The term is attested from 1681. A 1585 translation of Nicolas de Nicolay's 1576 Les navigations, peregrinations et voyages faicts en la Turquie includes \"the tulbant [turban] of the merchant must be skie coloured\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Shades_of_light_blue.png/330px-Shades_of_light_blue.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sky_blue","wikidata":"Q373160"},{"title":"Sky","blocks":[{"text":"The sky is an unobstructed view upward from the surface of the Earth. It includes the atmosphere and outer space. It may also be considered a place between the ground and outer space, thus distinct from outer space."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/July_night_sky_%2835972569256%29.jpg/330px-July_night_sky_%2835972569256%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sky","wikidata":"Q527"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue","wikidata":"Q1088"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Calmness_captured_in_blues.jpg/500px-Calmness_captured_in_blues.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Calmness_captured_in_blues.jpg/1280px-Calmness_captured_in_blues.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Calmness_captured_in_blues.jpg/500px-Calmness_captured_in_blues.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cumulus clouds showing vertical development against a clear sky.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACalmness_captured_in_blues.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Celeste_puro_tra_sole_e_orizzonte_a_Torregrotta.jpg/500px-Celeste_puro_tra_sole_e_orizzonte_a_Torregrotta.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Celeste_puro_tra_sole_e_orizzonte_a_Torregrotta.jpg/1280px-Celeste_puro_tra_sole_e_orizzonte_a_Torregrotta.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Celeste_puro_tra_sole_e_orizzonte_a_Torregrotta.jpg/500px-Celeste_puro_tra_sole_e_orizzonte_a_Torregrotta.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Pure Celeste between Spadafora and Torregrotta, Sicily in September; the colour of the ideal sky is shown with a perfect or near-perfect weather, especially close to the horizon, where the cyan is more evident.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACeleste_puro_tra_sole_e_orizzonte_a_Torregrotta.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Celeste_puro_tra_sole_e_orizzonte.jpg/500px-Celeste_puro_tra_sole_e_orizzonte.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Celeste_puro_tra_sole_e_orizzonte.jpg/1280px-Celeste_puro_tra_sole_e_orizzonte.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Celeste_puro_tra_sole_e_orizzonte.jpg/500px-Celeste_puro_tra_sole_e_orizzonte.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Pure Celeste between Spadafora and Torregrotta, Sicily, with perfectly clear, serene and sunny weather in September. The pure celeste is more evident close to the horizon, where the cyan is more intense.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACeleste_puro_tra_sole_e_orizzonte.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Celeste_puro_all%27orizzonte_di_Messina.jpg/500px-Celeste_puro_all%27orizzonte_di_Messina.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Celeste_puro_all%27orizzonte_di_Messina.jpg/1280px-Celeste_puro_all%27orizzonte_di_Messina.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Celeste_puro_all%27orizzonte_di_Messina.jpg/500px-Celeste_puro_all%27orizzonte_di_Messina.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Pure celeste at the horizon of Messina, Sicily, in February; in this part of the year, with a relatively low Sun, the pure celeste is shown only at the horizon and around noon.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACeleste_puro_all'orizzonte_di_Messina.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Blue_Grotto%2C_Capri%2C_Italy.jpg/500px-Blue_Grotto%2C_Capri%2C_Italy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Blue_Grotto%2C_Capri%2C_Italy.jpg/1280px-Blue_Grotto%2C_Capri%2C_Italy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Blue_Grotto%2C_Capri%2C_Italy.jpg/500px-Blue_Grotto%2C_Capri%2C_Italy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Deep sky blue waters of the Blue Grotto in Capri, namesake of the original (and ongoing) name for this colour","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wik